From a4e7067456c71cc9cfab586ef145570ae686a72c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:04:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ingress: hold a declared VERIFY_EXISTING predecessor to this
 repository's recorded admissions

StegVerse-Labs/.github#3369 gap 2 ("stale head / fence"), the head half:
option 2A of design/INGRESS_GAP_OPTIONS_3369.md. The lineage contract
(docs/CANONICAL_NODE_INGRESS_CONTRACT_001.json) says the receiving boundary
must validate the predecessor; node_standing.require checks its shape and
successor arithmetic only, and nothing on the receive() path compared a
declared predecessor with anything this organization had recorded.

Two changes:
- sdk_manifest_crossing.cross() returns the standing the packet carried
  ("standing": node_ref, mode, generation, predecessor), so an admission's
  repository receipt names the chain position it was admitted at. Replay
  identity is unchanged (request_sha256); recorded receipts are read as-is.
- receive() checks, before cross(), a declared standing in VERIFY_EXISTING
  mode whose generation is predecessor.generation + 1 and whose
  predecessor.manifest_sha256 is well-formed, against this repository's
  ledger (read once, never written): an admission for the same node_ref at
  predecessor.generation -- a repository receipt whose organization receipt
  is observed -- recorded under that manifest digest must exist (FAIL_CLOSED
  DECLARED_PREDECESSOR_NOT_RECORDED otherwise, also when the chain cannot be
  read), and no other recorded successor of the node may already bind that
  predecessor (DENY DECLARED_PREDECESSOR_SUPERSEDED). Predicate
  DECLARED_PREDECESSOR_IS_RECORDED_AND_UNSUPERSEDED_IN_THIS_LEDGER, owner
  ORGANIZATION-BATCH-CUSTODY-REPLAY-001 (the readback owner the spec_gap
  names), six fields, recorded at both ledger levels. Genesis is untouched;
  a genesis recorded without a generation key is generation 1. Shape and
  arithmetic refusals stay the standing contract's own at the boundary. A
  redelivery of a recorded admission is that admission (I-10).

What is compared, and what is not:
- The digest matches either recorded form of the admission's manifest --
  wire_manifest_sha256, which is what the SDK's successor_predecessor_binding
  produces over a manifest body, or canonical_manifest_sha256 of the
  validated projection -- since both name the same admission.
- An admission recorded before the crossing result carried its standing has
  no node or generation to compare; it matches on the digest alone and the
  result says so (declared_predecessor_record:
  MANIFEST_DIGEST_ONLY_RECEIPT_PREDATES_RECORDED_STANDING, else
  NODE_GENERATION_AND_MANIFEST_DIGEST_RECORDED), so successors of existing
  chains are not stranded.
- result_sha256 is held to shape only: no receipt records a result digest.
  The result says so (declared_predecessor_result_binding:
  NOT_CHECKED_RESULT_DIGEST_NOT_RECORDED_IN_RECEIPTS).
- Only this repository's own admissions are read. A predecessor admitted into
  the organization ledger through another repository's ingress is not found
  here; that scope is named in n4's spec_gap for the readback owner.

Independently reviewed before export; the review's findings (digest artifact,
legacy receipts, genesis without generation, partial commits counted as
admissions, repeated chain walks) are fixed and pinned by tests.

tests/test_organization_ingress_declared_predecessor.py (21 tests) drives the
real receive(), crossing and process_boundary.py through genesis -> successor
-> successor chains, unrecorded / other-node / other-generation predecessors,
a forked second successor, redelivery, legacy receipts, a partial commit, an
unreadable chain, a single walk per ingress, and the boundary keeping its own
arithmetic refusal. n4's spec_gap now records both halves as implemented;
what remains is the result-digest binding, routed to the readback owner.

Refs StegVerse-Labs/.github#3369, #3195

